  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Win the ball in the board channel",
  "description": "Full rink with a goalkeeper in each goal. Place a line of cones a little way in from the right board in the opposition half, making a channel along the board. B (wide half) stands down by their own end line, A (forward or midfielder) in the middle of their own half and the defender X centrally up by the centre line.\n\nThe goalkeeper throws out to B, who picks up speed along the board. B carries the ball a few metres and hits a hard ground pass forward along the board to A, who is skating at speed from the middle out towards the board. A takes the ball into the channel and tries to keep the speed all the way to goal. X sets off at the same time as A, comes in at an angle from behind, steers A towards the board and wins the ball. The drill ends when X has cleared or A has shot.\n\nRun it from both sides and swap roles after a few turns. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "X: do not get in front of the attacker – stay just behind and inside and steer them towards the board."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "X: take the ball when it is furthest from the attacker's stick, then clear it away from goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A: keep your speed through the channel and shield the ball with your body."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "B: a hard ground pass that does not bounce, in front of A in their skating line."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
